 "key": "F major",
 "bpm": 138,
 "concept": "\"Don's Theme\": a lilting music-box waltz in F major at 138 bpm (one bar = 1.30 s). The celesta sings a short, catchy theme (A-C | D-C | A-Bb-C | G) over a warm pad, harp 'pah-pah' plucks and a soft round bass; a few two-beat bars realign the downbeats so harmony changes land on the facade (6.09), the punch-in (15.65), the cream splash (26.96), the burst (32.17) and the logo (36.5). The DON'S letters are mickey-moused by a rising F-A-C-D-E line that resolves to F on the punch-in; the build climbs (bass Bb-C-D-C, melody up to G6) into a C7sus4 swell, falls to near-silence for the fireworks, and returns through Bbmaj7-Am7-Bb/C to a final F major bell chord on the logo.",
